# Day 41

## Experiment Title

Understanding Workflow Triggers in GitHub Actions


## Objective

To study different workflow triggers used in GitHub Actions for automating tasks.


## Theory

Workflow triggers are events that automatically start GitHub Actions workflows. These triggers allow workflows to run when specific activities occur inside a repository such as push events, pull requests, issue creation, or manual execution.

GitHub Actions uses YAML configuration files to define workflow triggers and automation steps. Workflow automation improves development efficiency and reduces manual effort during software integration and testing.


## Requirements

GitHub Account

GitHub Repository

GitHub Actions

Windows Operating System


## Procedure

Open the GitHub repository.

Access the workflow configuration file.

Study different workflow trigger events supported by GitHub Actions.

Configure workflow triggers for repository events.

Push changes to the repository and observe workflow execution.

Verify automatic workflow activation after repository updates.


## Output

Workflow triggers were configured successfully in GitHub Actions.

The workflow executed automatically after repository events occurred.

Automation tasks were performed successfully through workflow triggers.


## Result

Successfully understood workflow triggers and automation in GitHub Actions.
